ITEM C, D, G EXECUTION LOG
==========================

ITEM C — Era adjustment resolution
Resolution: WITHDRAW the era-adjusted column.
Rationale:
1. The formula raw_ratio * (30yr / era) holds gauge fixed while substituting 30-year CHIRPS
   in the denominator. This assumes the gauge does not track the anomaly — the opposite
   of the stated assumption that gauge and satellite co-vary.
2. Because both numerator and denominator are matched to the exact same years, interannual
   and decadal wetness anomalies affect both and largely cancel out in the ratio.
3. Adjusting one side externally introduces an uncalibrated counterfactual rather than a
   defensible adjustment. Period bias is controlled by period-matching.

ITEM D — Wetness regression at Mahabaleshwar
n: 5
