intercept: 6.180246
r: -0.523148 (approx -0.523)
p: 0.365679 (approx 0.37)
stderr: 0.00155725
sum_of_squared_ratio_deviations: 2.9702
Confirmation: Independent check values confirmed:
  r = -0.523 (confirmed)
  p ≈ 0.37 (confirmed: 0.366)
  slope ≈ -0.00166 ratio/mm (confirmed: -0.001656)
  sum of squared ratio deviations = 2.9702 (confirmed: 2.9702)
Interpretation:
  The gauge-to-CHIRPS bias factor shows no statistically detectable dependence
  on seasonal wetness (p = 0.37 >> 0.05). However, with n = 5, statistical power
  is very low, so failure to reject the null cannot be taken as proof of independence.

ITEM G — Month-specific fill
Summary Table:
Station              Raw (LB)   Old adj (season)    New adj (month)     Change
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Mahabaleshwar           3.381              3.860              3.789     -0.071
Kolhapur                1.564              1.866              1.862     -0.004
Belgaum/Sambra          0.935              1.120              1.099     -0.021
Sholapur                1.163              1.370              1.375     +0.005

Direction of movement:
  For Mahabaleshwar (-0.071), Belgaum (-0.021), and Kolhapur (-0.004), the adjusted ratio
  moves downward because missing days concentrate in drier shoulder months (June and September).
  For Sholapur (+0.005), missing days are evenly distributed across months.

Upper-estimate characterisation:
  Because the month-specific fill directly accounts for lower precipitation rates at season edges,
  the systematic upward bias of uniform season-mean scaling is eliminated. The 'upper estimate'
  characterisation is no longer required at the same strength, though the filled value remains a
  modelled sensitivity rather than a direct measurement.

Raw ratios confirmation:
  Raw ratios (3.381 / 1.564 / 0.935 / 1.163) remain strictly unchanged.
